<TextPage
	title="DMCA Takedown Policy | eCamx"
	description="How to report copyright infringement on eCamx. We remove listings on valid notice and forward reports to the originating cam platform."
	heading="DMCA Takedown Policy"
	updated="16 August 2026"
>
	<p>
		eCamx respects copyright. Because we are a directory that links to and embeds
		streams hosted by third-party platforms, the fastest route to removing
		infringing material is usually a notice to the platform that hosts it —
		but we will always remove the listing on our side as well.
	</p>

	<h2>How to file a notice</h2>
	<p>
		Send your notice to <a href="mailto:info@ecamx.com">info@ecamx.com</a>.
		To be actionable it must include:
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Identification of the copyrighted work you claim has been infringed.</li>
		<li>
			The exact eCamx URL of the listing at issue — a category or search page
			is not enough, we need the specific page.
		</li>
		<li>Your name, address, telephone number and email address.</li>
		<li>
			A statement that you have a good-faith belief that the use is not
			authorised by the copyright owner, its agent, or the law.
		</li>
		<li>
			A statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information in the notice
			is accurate and that you are the copyright owner or authorised to act on
			the owner's behalf.
		</li>
		<li>Your physical or electronic signature.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What we do with it</h2>
	<p>
		We aim to disable the reported listing within 48 hours of receiving a
		complete notice, and we forward the report to the platform that originates
		the stream. Note that removing a listing from eCamx does not remove the
		underlying stream — only the hosting platform can do that.
	</p>

	<h2>Counter-notice</h2>
	<p>
		If you believe your material was removed in error, send a counter-notice to
		the same address with the removed URL, your contact details, a statement
		under penalty of perjury that the removal was a mistake or misidentification,
		and your consent to the jurisdiction of the relevant courts. We may restore
		the listing after forwarding your counter-notice to the original complainant.
	</p>

	<h2>Repeat infringers</h2>
	<p>
		We permanently exclude sources that are the subject of repeated valid
		infringement notices.
	</p>

	<h2>A note on scope</h2>
	<p>
		eCamx hosts no video files and stores no images. Thumbnails and streams are
		served directly by the originating platform. Notices that concern the content
		of a live broadcast itself should go to that platform, which is named on
		every listing page.
	</p>
</TextPage>
